; The herd worker wall, macOS (Seatbelt / sandbox-exec). walls/darwin.sh renders this
; template from the neutral profile herd-spawn.sh writes to $HERD_DIR/walls/<name>/profile:
; each @@...@@ line below is replaced by the rules for one verb of that profile, and every
; other line is copied as it stands. In this language a LATER rule wins over an earlier
; one, so the order is the policy: allow everything, take every write away, give back the
; worker's own places, take back the few paths inside them it must not write, then deny
; the reads it must never make.
;
; Wall v1 permits the network. The ONE place wall v2 puts an egress policy is the last
; marker line below (the egress marker appears once in this file and in no other file under
; walls/); today it renders as a comment saying egress is open, and herd-spawn.sh refuses
; HERD_WALL_EGRESS=deny until the loopback proxy that policy needs exists.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny file-write*)
@@ALLOW_WRITE@@
@@DENY_WRITE@@
@@DENY_READ@@
@@EGRESS_POLICY@@
